334
00:12:04,920 --> 00:12:07,440
and in happiness for eternity one day.

335
00:12:07,440 --> 00:12:09,960
Which could be true, but it sure sounds like just what

336
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:12,560
people want to believe.

337
00:12:12,560 --> 00:12:15,360
Sounds like what you hope is true.

338
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:17,080
And the pets, will your dogs be there?

339
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:18,520
Definitely.

340
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:20,840
All your beloved pets will be there in heaven.

341
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:23,000
They don't go to dog heaven, a segregated heaven.

342
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:26,600
It wouldn't be heaven if your pet dog wasn't there.

343
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:28,840
Not the mean dogs.

344
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:29,920
They're somewhere else.

345
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:35,880
Now, rationality as political evolution.

346
00:12:35,880 --> 00:12:38,040
We got to the level of being slightly rational,

347
00:12:38,040 --> 00:12:39,680
but we'll do it.

348
00:12:39,680 --> 00:12:43,640
So you may have noticed a pure technical tone to many things

349
00:12:43,640 --> 00:12:45,180
that I've said about people's beliefs,

350
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:47,400
and I will confess, as guilty as charged,

351
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:48,800
I am a puritan on these matters.

352
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:51,280
But as an economist, we don't just

353
00:12:51,280 --> 00:12:52,740
count the pure technical pleasures,

354
00:12:52,740 --> 00:12:55,520
we count the assorted pleasures as well.

355
00:12:55,520 --> 00:12:58,560
And what this means is that if we

356
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:02,040
