476
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:16,400
and would do almost anything to get it.

477
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:18,400
So they're competing.

478
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:20,920
They're competing through by hook or by crook,

479
00:17:20,920 --> 00:17:23,480
with any method they can get their hands on.

480
00:17:23,480 --> 00:17:25,440
Like, what would it take before they would say,

481
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:26,760
oh, no, it's too far.

482
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:28,640
Too far.

483
00:17:28,640 --> 00:17:30,640
All right, so the monopoly story doesn't seem,

484
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:32,080
it seems very weak.

485
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:33,840
And again, this high transactions cost one,

486
00:17:33,840 --> 00:17:35,960
I think Whitman makes some very good points there.

487
00:17:35,960 --> 00:17:38,360
It's just a matter of high transactions cost one.

488
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:39,560
We just say, all right, fine.

489
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:41,600
Let's go and bundle a bunch of policies

490
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:44,400
together to get the transactions cost down.

491
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:47,480
Or let's go and delegate more power

492
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:51,520
to a smaller number of people to overcome the transactions cost.

493
00:17:51,520 --> 00:17:55,160
And I say, this is the one where Whitman is totally wrong,

494
00:17:55,160 --> 00:17:58,160
which ruins the rest of his arguments, which

495
00:17:58,160 --> 00:18:00,880
is that the key actors in his model of the voters

496
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:03,760
are nothing like what he talks about.

497
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:06,040
They're not people with rational expectations.

498
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:08,720
They're not people who just have a problem with ignorance.

499
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:11,160
They're people who turn the common sense dial down

500
00:18:11,160 --> 00:18:12,880
to near zero.

501
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:16,880
And when you do that, then you get endless nonsense.

502
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:18,800
So Tyler would point out that's a little bit,

503
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:19,680
that's hyperbole two.

504
00:18:19,680 --> 00:18:20,480
It's not endless.

505
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:23,200
High levels of nonsense.

506
00:18:23,200 --> 00:18:26,480
But technically, endless just means that it hasn't ended yet.

507
00:18:26,480 --> 00:18:29,000
So I don't think, and also a prediction

508
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:30,200
that it's not going to end.

509
00:18:30,200 --> 00:18:31,880
The nonsense will continue.

510
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:33,680
50 years from now, if you're still alive

511
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:36,840
and you open a newspaper, you think everything will,

